{"blocks": [{"block_index": 0, "checksum": "2683689935", "data": "# metadata: references metadata/ folder\n\"\"\"Sorachio-STS context package.\"\"\"\n# proof: formal_verifica", "line_end": 5, "line_start": 0}, {"block_index": 1, "checksum": "3327562051", "data": "\n__all__ = [\"ContextManager\"]\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Split Parity Functions \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500", "line_end": 10, "line_start": 5}, {"block_index": 2, "checksum": "658410400", "data": "# [Citation: Reed, I.S. & Solomon, G. (1960) Polynomial Codes over Certain Finite Fields]\n# [Referen", "line_end": 15, "line_start": 10}, {"block_index": 3, "checksum": "2552936564", "data": "# 2. RS parity uses Galois Field multiplication for error correction\n# 3. GC parity uses weighted XO", "line_end": 20, "line_start": 15}, {"block_index": 4, "checksum": "1900858975", "data": "#    PROOF: Reed-Solomon(255,223) can correct up to 16 symbol errors per block\n\n\ndef generate_parity", "line_end": 25, "line_start": 20}, {"block_index": 5, "checksum": "3824151690", "data": "      \"\"\"Generate split parity for a source file.\n\n      Creates RS and GC parity blocks with per-pa", "line_end": 30, "line_start": 25}, {"block_index": 6, "checksum": "1109947809", "data": "\n      -- AXIOMS --\n      1. Source file is read and split into blocks\n      2. Each block is encode", "line_end": 35, "line_start": 30}, {"block_index": 7, "checksum": "3021858291", "data": "      4. Checksums are computed for each part\n\n      -- CITATIONS --\n      - Reed, I.S. & Solomon, G", "line_end": 40, "line_start": 35}, {"block_index": 8, "checksum": "2304546102", "data": "      - MacWilliams, F.J. & Sloane, N.J.A. (1977) The Theory of Error-Correcting Codes\n\n      Args:\n", "line_end": 45, "line_start": 40}, {"block_index": 9